# Implementation Plan - Master & Lookup Tables Knowledge Base Redesign

Redesign the SQL Agent knowledge base, database metadata extractor, relationship discovery, business semantics engine, and hybrid retriever to treat master and lookup tables (specifically `user_role` alongside 8 existing tables) as first-class citizens.

## Overview & Technical Objectives
Currently, the agent uses an 8-table scope and lacks understanding of lookup/master tables like `user_role`. When a user asks a business question like `"Retailer scan count in Jan 2026"`, the model mistakenly generates `WHERE user_role = 'retailer'` instead of joining `users` to `user_role` or applying the discovered integer code mapping (`user_role = 5` / `user_role.id = 5`).

This plan redesigns the knowledge base to:
1. Expand target database scope to **9 tables**: `users`, `user_role` (mapped to physical `role` table), `wallet_transaction`, `sku_inventories`, `companies`, `machine_details`, `withdrawal_request`, `automatic_transactions`, `automate`.
2. Automatically detect Primary Keys, Foreign Keys, Lookup/Master tables, Enum columns, and Business Meanings using MySQL read-only metadata (`INFORMATION_SCHEMA`, `SHOW TABLES`, `SHOW COLUMNS`, `SHOW INDEX`).
3. Capture **ALL rows** for lookup/master tables (`user_role`) during training/knowledge generation to dynamically build a **Business Dictionary** (`Retailer` $\rightarrow$ `user_role.id = 5`, `Distributor` $\rightarrow$ `user_role.id = 2`, `Dealer` $\rightarrow$ `user_role.id = 3`, `Company` $\rightarrow$ `user_role.id = 4`).
4. Discover relationships (e.g. `users.user_role` $\rightarrow$ `user_role.id`, `wallet_transaction.user_id` $\rightarrow$ `users.id`) without hardcoding or guessing joins.
5. Perform **Hybrid Retrieval** supplying relevant tables, discovered relationships, lookup table data, business mappings, and SQL examples.
6. Provide an automated, read-only **Knowledge Builder** (`app/knowledge/knowledge_builder.py`) to rebuild the knowledge base on schema changes.

---

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> **Database Table Mapping (`user_role` vs `role`)**: In the MySQL target database (`jghMasterDB`), the physical role lookup table is named `role`. The system will map `user_role` as the canonical master table entity and automatically translate `user_role` references in queries to `role` if required, keeping full backward and forward compatibility.
> All database access will remain **strictly READ-ONLY** (`SELECT` and `INFORMATION_SCHEMA` queries).

